{
  "duration": 60.819,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.139,
      "text": "So welcome back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.48,
      "end": 4.079,
      "text": "I hope you have gone through the theory part for this topic."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.44,
      "end": 5.98,
      "text": "Now it's time to solve some problems."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.379,
      "end": 8.0,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.34,
      "end": 9.36,
      "text": "the speed of a train is"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.8,
      "end": 11.279,
      "text": "seventy-two kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.88,
      "end": 15.639,
      "text": "The question is asking us to convert the speed into meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.059,
      "end": 19.759,
      "text": "Now, before solving, let us recall one basic conversion."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.219,
      "end": 25.619,
      "text": "We know that one kilometer per hour is equal to five by eighteen meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.18,
      "end": 28.779,
      "text": "This is a direct formula-based question."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.199,
      "end": 32.559,
      "text": "So we simply multiply the given speed by five by eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.04,
      "end": 39.0,
      "text": "Speed in meters per second is equal to speed in kilometers per hour into five by eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.36,
      "end": 40.719,
      "text": "Now, putting the given value,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.099,
      "end": 43.84,
      "text": "speed is equal to seventy-two into five by eighteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.2,
      "end": 45.239,
      "text": "After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.559,
      "end": 50.959,
      "text": "seventy-two divided by eighteen becomes four. So we get four into five, which is twenty."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.279,
      "end": 55.099,
      "text": "Hence, the speed of the train is twenty meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.419,
      "end": 58.059,
      "text": "So the final answer is twenty meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.5,
      "end": 60.819,
      "text": "Hence, the correct option is option A."
    }
  ],
